\f0 \b \fs28 \pard \s10 \li1209 \fi-1007 \ri1007 \ql Class Description\
\fs14\
\f1 \b0 \fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 An NSTextField is a kind of NSControl that displays text that the user can select or edit, and which sends its action message to its target when the user presses the Return key while editing. Like other controls, it also performs validation on its value when edited; if the value isn\'27t valid it sends a special error action message to its target. An NSTextField can be assigned a delegate, who is then informed of delegate messages sent by the window\'27s field editor, such as \b textShouldEndEditing:\b0 . See the NSWindow and NSTextView class specifications for more information on a window\'27s field editor.\
\fs14\
\fs28 Typical of several kinds of control, NSTextField allows you to set its text and background color, whether it draws the background, and whether it draws a bezel or border around its text. Note that the text and background colors of selected text are configurable. The selected text color overshadows any actual text color applied to the text while it\'27s selected (this is generally the case with controls).\
\fs14\
\fs28 You can link text fields together in their window\'27s key view loop, as described in the NSWindow class specification. \
\fs14\
